[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4282567756","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118584#issuecomment-4282567756","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118584","id":4282567756,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_QsxM","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-20T16:30:58Z","updated_at":"2026-04-20T16:30:58Z","body":"It's definitely a little usual to have a class that is only built in editor builds to be registered at the scene level, but I wouldn't necessarily say it's \"wrong\"\r\n\r\nIf you register it at the editor level, then it'll only be available if the editor is launched (ie `godot --editor`). Whereas registering it at the scene level will mean it's available in game, but only in editor builds.\r\n\r\nI know there are folks that want to be able to script lightmap baking. I don't recall if that's currently possible (or just a requested feature), and I don't know if the `LightmapRD` class is necessary to do it, but that use case would probably require that the necessary classes are registered at the scene level","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4282567756/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4284511498","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/118584#issuecomment-4284511498","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/118584","id":4284511498,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7_YHUK","user":{"login":"neikeq","id":7718100,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjc3MTgxMDA=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7718100?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq","html_url":"https://github.com/neikeq","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/neikeq/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-20T21:50:40Z","updated_at":"2026-04-20T21:50:40Z","body":"It's technically wrong at least for C# because, as a statically compiled language, if using the type doesn't produce any compiler error, then it shouldn't produce a runtime error either.\r\n\r\nBut since this is not a fatal issue, and the change could break compatibility, and some people might be depending on this for valid use cases, I don't think it's worth pursuing further.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4284511498/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]